  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "DxKnfXHOMI/TLKZdYqMYY0x5yfM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:34:05.366Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`switchboard-lb` is an OpenResty (nginx + Lua) load balancer whose whole routing decision is one header. In the nginx **rewrite phase** \u2014 after headers are parsed, before the upstream is chosen \u2014 a two-line Lua module copies the `Drive-Id` request header (exposed by nginx as `$http_drive_id`) into `$doc_id`, and the upstream block's `hash $doc_id consistent` reads it when picking a backend.\n\nFive header rules make up the contract:\n\n1. `Drive-Id` becomes `$doc_id`.\n2. **Empty or missing header \u2192 round-robin.** An empty hash key falls back to round-robin across the peers (documented nginx behaviour), which serves legacy clients and any operation with no single owning drive \u2014 `node` queries by id, introspection, the supergraph's `_service` call.\n3. **The header is advisory.** The LB does not validate it; a misrouted request gets a *structured wrong-shard error* from the switchboard's drive-validation middleware (`packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/gateway/drive-middleware.ts`). Routing is optimistic, correctness lives downstream.\n4. **No body inspection.** The LB never calls `ngx.req.read_body()` on `/graphql`; bodies stream straight through. This is what lets it stay agnostic to POST, GET-with-query, request batches, persisted queries and future schema changes.\n5. **The header name is part of the contract** \u2014 renaming it is a coordinated client-and-server change.\n\nAn earlier implementation *did* parse the body to find a document id and rejected header-less requests with `409 Conflict`. That model, and the `lua/errors.lua` that powered it, were deleted: under the header model the LB never needs a routing key for correctness, so round-robin is both safe and strictly more useful than rejecting.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/switchboard-lb/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 \u00a74.1 Route classes; \u00a74.3 Header rules; \u00a79 Q5 (decided 2026-05-05)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:34:05.366Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:34:05.366Z"
    }
  },
